From 6777c8573d5e3d53d36268fbcfb4c2f6a9f5965d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John O'Dell <johncodell14@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:35:51 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] civ45: siege units wound whole stacks, fights go to the
 death, fast units break off, bombard range 1

Catapult, Cannon, Artillery and Howitzer get the Collateral flag and a
bombard_rate (5, 10, 14, 20). "Bombard 2", Freeciv's non-lethal bombard,
is enabled for them against an adjacent tile that holds two or more
enemy units, so every unit there is shot at and wounded but none is
killed; against a lone unit they attack as before, and against a stack
the player may still attack instead. Bombarding ends the unit's turn.

Combat_Rounds drops from 15 to 0, so a fight lasts until one side dies,
except for attackers with the new Withdraws flag (Horsemen, Chariot,
Elephants, Crusaders, Knights, Dragoons, Cavalry, Armor), whose attack
ends after 12 rounds for every 10 hit points they have left. Aircraft
bombard reaches one tile again instead of two. README.civ45, the
summary and the flag help texts describe the rules.
---
 data/civ45/README.civ45    | 16 ++++++-
 data/civ45/actions.ruleset | 95 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 data/civ45/effects.ruleset | 52 ++++++++++++++++++++-
 data/civ45/game.ruleset    | 10 ++--
 data/civ45/units.ruleset   | 30 +++++++-----
 5 files changed, 178 insertions(+), 25 deletions(-)

diff --git a/data/civ45/README.civ45 b/data/civ45/README.civ45
index 01fe760..2940126 100644
--- a/data/civ45/README.civ45
+++ b/data/civ45/README.civ45
@@ -28,7 +28,21 @@ Differences from sandbox
 - The ruleset suggests the trident tileset, the only overhead square
   tileset Freeciv ships, until a Freeciv45 tileset exists.
 - Cultural victory is enabled alongside spacerace and allied victory.
-- Bombard range is 2 instead of 1.
+- Combat is to the death: a fight lasts until the attacker or the
+  defender dies (sandbox stops every fight after 15 rounds). Units with
+  the Withdraws flag (Horsemen, Chariot, Elephants, Crusaders, Knights,
+  Dragoons, Cavalry, Armor) break off their own attacks instead, after
+  12 rounds for every 10 hit points they have left; when attacked they
+  fight to the death like everyone else.
+- Siege collateral: Catapult, Cannon, Artillery and Howitzer (flag
+  Collateral) can bombard an adjacent tile that holds two or more enemy
+  units ("Bombard Stack"). Every unit there is shot at bombard_rate
+  times (5, 10, 14, 20) and loses 1 hit point per hit, but none can be
+  killed by it (each keeps at least 1 hit point). Bombarding ends the
+  siege unit's turn. Against a lone unit the siege unit attacks as
+  usual, and against a stack the player may still choose to attack.
+- Bombard range is 1 for aircraft (sandbox's value; the first slices had
+  2 for ranged units of a different game).
 - Strategic resources: Legion needs Iron and Armor needs Oil somewhere in
   the city's radius.
 - Nation-unique units and buildings: Aztec Jaguar Warrior (replaces
